            <h2 id="now" class="doc-h2">Now</h2>
            <p class="doc-body">Current: a part description can be typed and saved on an order line. No STL is created yet. No template is added per part.</p>
            <p class="doc-body">Blocked by: port 4003 was not running. This file is not served until that server is up and Documentation is rescanned. Do not start the server from this plan.</p>
            <p class="doc-body">Done: <a href="[% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %]?record_id=2681" class="doc-link">todo #2681</a> stores any part description on the order line. Next is <a href="[% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %]?record_id=2682" class="doc-link">todo #2682</a>, optional pictures. No STL is created yet.</p>
            <div class="doc-navrow">
                <a href="[% c.uri_for('/project/details') %]?project_id=310" class="doc-navlink">Project #310</a>
                <a href="[% c.uri_for('/todo') %]?project_id=310" class="doc-navlink">Todos</a>
                <a href="[% c.uri_for('/CustomerOrder/new') %]" class="doc-navlink">Customer order form</a>
            </div>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="decisions" class="doc-h2">Decisions</h2>
            <p class="doc-body">Corrected 2026-11-07. Type any description. An STL comes back. No new program is checked in for that part.</p>
            <table class="doc-table">
                <tr>
                    <th class="doc-th">Decision</th>
                    <th class="doc-th">Resolution</th>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td class="doc-td">Units</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">29 cm and 33 cm are circumferences. Tube length is 42 cm. Convert with diameter_mm = circumference_cm * 10 / pi. Do not treat 29 as a diameter.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="doc-tr-alt">
                    <td class="doc-td">Collar length</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">4 cm (40 mm) for this fixture. Staff can change it. The fit check still refuses a length that cannot slide on from the small end.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td class="doc-td">Who generates</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Staff and admin only, until this is proven. The customer submits words and pictures.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="doc-tr-alt">
                    <td class="doc-td">Voice</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Text only. A microphone is a future option, not this project.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td class="doc-td">Any description</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Staff type the part in words. The tool writes a one-off solid for that request, renders it with the existing OpenSCAD service, and staff accept or reject the STL. Do not add a template file per shape.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="doc-tr-alt">
                    <td class="doc-td">Tracking</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Child project #310 under #206. Not under #272. #272 is the dryer import project.</td>
                </tr>
            </table>
            <div class="doc-warning">
                <p class="doc-body">Treating a 29 cm circumference as a 29 mm diameter prints a ring about one-third the real size. The desk must show the converted diameters, about 92.3 mm and 105.0 mm, before it renders.</p>
            </div>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="workflow" class="doc-h2">Staff workflow</h2>
            <p class="doc-body">Staff type any description. The tool returns an STL for that request only. A collar is one example, not the product.</p>
            <ol class="doc-body">
                <li>Staff type the description. Pictures can be attached as reference. They are not required.</li>
                <li>The app asks the existing AI catalog for OpenSCAD source for that description. That source is not saved as a new template.</li>
                <li>The existing OpenSCAD service renders it. The service already accepts scad_source on POST /render and returns STL bytes.</li>
                <li>Staff look at the result and accept or reject it. Accept saves a printing_3d_models row. Reject saves nothing.</li>
                <li>A shape the solid generator cannot build shows the error. It does not invent a mesh from a photo.</li>
            </ol>
            <div class="doc-warning">
                <p class="doc-body">This makes measured solids from words: a collar, a box, a bracket, a clip. It will not reliably make a figurine, a face, or a part that only exists in a photo. That would be a different tool, and this shop does not have one.</p>
            </div>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="fixture" class="doc-h2">Example description</h2>
            <p class="doc-body">The vacuum collar is one description to try, not a special template. A second, different description must also return an STL before this is called working. The numbers below are the customer's words. The generator has to read them. Do not hard-code a collar.</p>
            <table class="doc-table">
                <tr>
                    <th class="doc-th">Input</th>
                    <th class="doc-th">Customer figure</th>
                    <th class="doc-th">Used by the fit check</th>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td class="doc-td">Tube length</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">42 cm</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">420 mm</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="doc-tr-alt">
                    <td class="doc-td">Small end</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">29 cm circumference</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">about 92.31 mm diameter</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td class="doc-td">Large end</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">33 cm circumference</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">about 105.04 mm diameter</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="doc-tr-alt">
                    <td class="doc-td">Collar length</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">4 cm</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">40 mm</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td class="doc-td">Wall</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">not given</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">staff entry, printable range 1.2 to 8 mm</td>
                </tr>
            </table>
            <p class="doc-body">A 40 mm collar on that taper must pass. A collar as long as the tube must fail, because a tight full-length sleeve cannot slide on from the small end. The STL is the collar only.</p>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

